      "text": "Proof. Each ∆n-frieze F is a horizontal translation of a frieze F′ in its Z/P∆nZ-orbit such that Fi,1′ ≤ Fi,j′ for all 1 ≤ j ≤ P∆n. By Lemma 2.11, there is a bound on",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.19529248366013072,
        "y0": 0.8215429292929293,
        "x1": 0.3079297385620915,
        "y1": 0.8497386363636363
      },
      "text": "P∆n j=1 Fi,j′ ≤ bPi,∆∆n",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.176468954248366,
        "y0": 0.8239671717171717,
        "x1": 0.8234705882352941,
        "y1": 0.8916073232323233
      },
      "text": ". But xi = Fi,1′ is the smallest factor in the product of P∆n-many terms, hence xi ≤ bi,∆n. If the entries of F are all at least 2, then the entries of the translation F′ are also all at least 2. Hence the same argument gives the bound in terms of ci,∆n instead of bi,∆n.",
